config SAMPLE_HARDEN
	tristate "Buggy KCOV/KASAN hardening demo drivers"
	depends on KCOV && m
	help
	  Build two deliberately buggy misc-device drivers used by the
	  "KCOV + libFuzzer + KASAN" hands-on hardening tutorial:

	    harden_local  - parses a zero-copy shared page in syscall context
	                    (local KCOV coverage).
	    harden_remote - parses the same page on a workqueue kthread
	                    (remote KCOV coverage, KCOV_REMOTE_ENABLE).

	  Both contain a write-side out-of-bounds bug behind an under-covered
	  branch, intended to be found by the userspace libFuzzer harnesses in
	  tools/harden/sample/. Do NOT enable on a production kernel.

	  If unsure, say N.
